  Cell["Pure simplicial complexes with q facets of size p: exact enumeration, \
statistics and distributions", "Subtitle"], Cell["To start: Evaluation \
\[FilledRightTriangle] Evaluate Notebook (or the button below). Needs Wolfram \
15 or later and this repository; ECGrav is taken from COMB_ECGRAV_DIR if set, \
else ECGrav-upstream next to run.wl, else the installed paclet.", "Text"], 
  Cell[BoxData[ButtonBox["\"Start: evaluate the notebook\"", 
     ButtonFunction :> FrontEndTokenExecute["EvaluateNotebook"], 
     ImageSize -> Automatic, Appearance -> Automatic, Evaluator -> Automatic, 
     Method -> "Preemptive"]], "Text"], Cell["The notebook only reads: it \
never writes into data/, figures/, logs/ or results/. Long jobs run on \
parallel kernels, show progress, and have a Stop button (Evaluation \
\[FilledRightTriangle] Abort Evaluation does the same, except while kernels \
are starting). The first job starts the kernels, which takes some seconds.", 
   "Text"], Cell["Get[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \
\"explorer_core.wl\"}]];\nGet[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \
\"explorer_panels.wl\"}]];", "Input", InitializationCell -> True], 
  Cell["ExplorerStatusPanel[]", "Input", InitializationCell -> True], 
  Cell["1. Enumerate", "Section"], Cell["EnumerateUnlabeledPureComplexes[p, \
q] lists one complex of every isomorphism class. Automatic is the McKay \
method for p \[GreaterEqual] 4 and Cheap below that. The table compares the \
number of classes with n vertices with ECGrav's NumUnlabeledPureComplexes \
and, where we have it, our stored truth. Start with (3, 4): 66 classes in a \
few seconds; (3, 5) takes minutes.", "Text"], 
  Cell["ExplorerEnumeratePanel[]", "Input", InitializationCell -> True], 
  Cell["2. Statistics", "Section"], Cell["PureComplexStatistics[complex, p] \
gives the 12 statistics named in $PureComplexStatisticNames. Take a complex \
from panel 1, draw one at random with ECGrav, or type one in. The first draw \
uniform over unlabeled complexes at a cell computes ECGrav's counts for it: \
about 20 s at (3, 10), minutes at (4, 9) and (4, 10). Later draws at the same \
cell are fast.", "Text"], Cell["ExplorerStatisticsPanel[]", "Input", 
   InitializationCell -> True], Cell["3. Exact distributions", "Section"], 
  Cell["PureComplexTruthMarginal[truth, target, statistic] gives the exact \
distribution of a statistic when the complex is uniform over unlabeled, \
facet-labeled or vertex-labeled complexes. A good start is (3, 5) with numV: \
the vertex-labeled distribution sits at much larger numbers of vertices than \
the other two. Cells marked stored are read from our truth files (data/ of \
the main checkout, else the copies in demo/data); the others are enumerated \
when you press Show.", "Text"], Cell["ExplorerDistributionPanel[]", "Input", 
